# The module version, and the source of the release tag.
#
# A merge to main that changes the version tags that commit as v<version>. A
# merge that leaves it alone tags nothing, so bump the version in the same pull
# request as the change it releases.
#
# Write a bare MAJOR.MINOR.PATCH version, with no leading zeros. The v belongs
# to the tag, not to this file. Releases only go up, so CI fails a pull request
# that lowers the version or picks one that already carries a tag.
#
# A # starts a comment anywhere on a line, and blank lines are ignored. What
# remains must be one version and nothing else.
#
# Raising the version here also means repointing the three `?ref=` pins in the
# README examples. Leave the `## Migrating to ...` heading alone: it names the
# release it describes, not the current one.
1.0.0
